From 4fd57cf8ca4d33c24413c9be40c8fa4ba1c25b61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 4evy <git@evy.pink>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0300
Subject: git fetch: refresh ancestry after shallow boundary changes

Allow regular fetches to deepen an existing shallow repository and add
the lower-level depth, deepen, and exclusion controls needed by raw-ref
fetches. Detect changes to the Git shallow boundary, refresh backend
caches, and rebuild the commit index so newly available ancestors are
immediately queryable, including after failed fetches

